{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Case Study 1: Hospital Readmission Prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "**Course:** Machine Learning Engineering (AI201B)  \n",
        "**Objective:** Predict whether a patient will be readmitted within 30 days.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Techniques used\n",
        "- Logistic Regression\n",
        "- L2 Regularization\n",
        "- Train/Test Split\n",
        "- Missing-value handling\n",
        "- One-hot encoding for categorical features\n",
        "- Feature scaling\n",
        "- ROC-AUC evaluation\n",
        "- Confusion Matrix\n",
        "- False Positive vs False Negative analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "**Target convention:** `1 = Readmitted`, `0 = Not Readmitted`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Import Libraries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from google.colab import files\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
        "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n",
        "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
        "    accuracy_score,\n",
        "    confusion_matrix,\n",
        "    classification_report,\n",
        "    roc_auc_score,\n",
        "    roc_curve,\n",
        "    precision_score,\n",
        "    recall_score,\n",
        "    f1_score\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Libraries imported successfully.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Upload Hospital Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "Run the cell below and choose your hospital CSV file."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
        "\n",
        "uploaded_filename = next(iter(uploaded))\n",
        "print(\"Uploaded file:\", uploaded_filename)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Load Dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df = pd.read_csv(uploaded_filename)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Dataset shape:\", df.shape)\n",
        "display(df.head())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Basic Data Exploration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Column names:\")\n",
        "print(df.columns.tolist())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nDataset information:\")\n",
        "df.info()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nMissing values:\")\n",
        "display(df.isnull().sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head(20))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Detect the Target Column\n",
        "\n",
        "The notebook checks common readmission target names automatically.\n",
        "\n",
        "If your dataset uses a different target name, edit `TARGET_COLUMN` manually."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "target_candidates = [\n",
        "    \"readmitted\",\n",
        "    \"Readmitted\",\n",
        "    \"readmission\",\n",
        "    \"Readmission\",\n",
        "    \"readmission_30\",\n",
        "    \"readmitted_30\",\n",
        "    \"30_day_readmission\",\n",
        "    \"readmission_30_days\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "TARGET_COLUMN = None\n",
        "\n",
        "for col in target_candidates:\n",
        "    if col in df.columns:\n",
        "        TARGET_COLUMN = col\n",
        "        break\n",
        "\n",
        "if TARGET_COLUMN is None:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"Target column not found automatically. \"\n",
        "        \"Please set TARGET_COLUMN manually to the column containing 0/1 readmission labels.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Target column:\", TARGET_COLUMN)\n",
        "print(\"\\nTarget value counts:\")\n",
        "print(df[TARGET_COLUMN].value_counts(dropna=False))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Prepare Target Values\n",
        "\n",
        "This cell converts common text labels such as `Yes/No` to `1/0` when necessary."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "y_raw = df[TARGET_COLUMN].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "if y_raw.dtype == \"object\":\n",
        "    mapping = {\n",
        "        \"yes\": 1,\n",
        "        \"y\": 1,\n",
        "        \"readmitted\": 1,\n",
        "        \"1\": 1,\n",
        "        \"true\": 1,\n",
        "        \"no\": 0,\n",
        "        \"n\": 0,\n",
        "        \"not readmitted\": 0,\n",
        "        \"0\": 0,\n",
        "        \"false\": 0\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    y_clean = (\n",
        "        y_raw.astype(str)\n",
        "             .str.strip()\n",
        "             .str.lower()\n",
        "             .map(mapping)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    if y_clean.isnull().any():\n",
        "        bad_values = y_raw[y_clean.isnull()].dropna().unique()[:10]\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\n",
        "            f\"Some target values could not be mapped automatically: {bad_values}. \"\n",
        "            \"Please encode the target manually as 0 and 1.\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    y = y_clean.astype(int)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    y = pd.to_numeric(y_raw, errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    if y.isnull().any():\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\"Target contains non-numeric or missing values.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    unique_values = sorted(pd.Series(y).unique().tolist())\n",
        "\n",
        "    if set(unique_values) == {0, 1}:\n",
        "        y = y.astype(int)\n",
        "    elif len(unique_values) == 2:\n",
        "        y = y.map({unique_values[0]: 0, unique_values[1]: 1}).astype(int)\n",
        "        print(\"Target was automatically converted to 0/1.\")\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\n",
        "            \"Target must contain exactly two classes for binary classification.\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "print(y.value_counts())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Separate Features and Target"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X = df.drop(columns=[TARGET_COLUMN]).copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Remove obvious ID-like columns if present\n",
        "id_like_columns = [\n",
        "    col for col in X.columns\n",
        "    if col.lower() in {\n",
        "        \"id\", \"patient_id\", \"patientid\", \"encounter_id\", \"encounterid\"\n",
        "    }\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "if id_like_columns:\n",
        "    print(\"Dropping ID-like columns:\", id_like_columns)\n",
        "    X = X.drop(columns=id_like_columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"X shape:\", X.shape)\n",
        "print(\"y shape:\", y.shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8. Train/Test Split\n",
        "\n",
        "`stratify=y` keeps approximately the same class ratio in both training and testing sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    test_size=0.20,\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    stratify=y\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Training set:\", X_train.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Testing set :\", X_test.shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 9. Build Preprocessing Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "- Numerical columns: median imputation + standardization\n",
        "- Categorical columns: most-frequent imputation + one-hot encoding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "numeric_features = X_train.select_dtypes(include=np.number).columns.tolist()\n",
        "categorical_features = X_train.select_dtypes(exclude=np.number).columns.tolist()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Numeric features:\", len(numeric_features))\n",
        "print(\"Categorical features:\", len(categorical_features))\n",
        "\n",
        "numeric_pipeline = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
        "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
        "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler())\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "categorical_pipeline = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
        "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n",
        "    (\"onehot\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\"))\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
        "    transformers=[\n",
        "        (\"num\", numeric_pipeline, numeric_features),\n",
        "        (\"cat\", categorical_pipeline, categorical_features)\n",
        "    ]\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 10. Logistic Regression with L2 Regularization\n",
        "\n",
        "L2 regularization penalizes large coefficients and helps reduce overfitting.\n",
        "\n",
        "`C` is the inverse of regularization strength:\n",
        "- smaller `C` → stronger regularization\n",
        "- larger `C` → weaker regularization"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "model = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
        "    (\"preprocessor\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"classifier\", LogisticRegression(\n",
        "        penalty=\"l2\",\n",
        "        C=1.0,\n",
        "        max_iter=2000,\n",
        "        solver=\"liblinear\",\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    ))\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Model trained successfully.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 11. Make Predictions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n",
        "y_prob = model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"First 10 predicted classes:\", y_pred[:10])\n",
        "print(\"First 10 readmission probabilities:\", np.round(y_prob[:10], 3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 12. Evaluation Metrics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Accuracy :\", round(accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred), 4))\n",
        "print(\"Precision:\", round(precision_score(y_test, y_pred, zero_division=0), 4))\n",
        "print(\"Recall   :\", round(recall_score(y_test, y_pred, zero_division=0), 4))\n",
        "print(\"F1 Score :\", round(f1_score(y_test, y_pred, zero_division=0), 4))\n",
        "print(\"ROC-AUC  :\", round(roc_auc_score(y_test, y_prob), 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nClassification Report:\")\n",
        "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred, zero_division=0))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 13. Confusion Matrix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)\n",
        "print(cm)\n",
        "\n",
        "tn, fp, fn, tp = cm.ravel()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nTrue Negative :\", tn)\n",
        "print(\"False Positive:\", fp)\n",
        "print(\"False Negative:\", fn)\n",
        "print(\"True Positive :\", tp)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Clinical Meaning\n",
        "\n",
        "- **False Negative (FN):** A patient who will be readmitted is predicted as low risk.  \n",
        "  This may be clinically costly because the patient could miss extra monitoring or follow-up.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **False Positive (FP):** A patient who will not be readmitted is predicted as high risk.  \n",
        "  This may cause unnecessary tests, follow-ups, or use of hospital resources."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 14. ROC Curve and ROC-AUC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fpr, tpr, thresholds = roc_curve(y_test, y_prob)\n",
        "auc_value = roc_auc_score(y_test, y_prob)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 5))\n",
        "plt.plot(fpr, tpr, label=f\"ROC-AUC = {auc_value:.3f}\")\n",
        "plt.plot([0, 1], [0, 1], linestyle=\"--\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"False Positive Rate\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"True Positive Rate\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"ROC Curve - Hospital Readmission\")\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 15. Try a Lower Decision Threshold\n",
        "\n",
        "In healthcare, lowering the threshold can increase recall and reduce false negatives, but it can also increase false positives."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "threshold = 0.40\n",
        "y_pred_040 = (y_prob >= threshold).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Threshold:\", threshold)\n",
        "print(\"Precision:\", round(precision_score(y_test, y_pred_040, zero_division=0), 4))\n",
        "print(\"Recall   :\", round(recall_score(y_test, y_pred_040, zero_division=0), 4))\n",
        "print(\"F1 Score :\", round(f1_score(y_test, y_pred_040, zero_division=0), 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nConfusion Matrix:\")\n",
        "print(confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred_040))"
      ]
    },
      ],
